  "version": "0.3.0",
  "title": "SG90 micro servo",
  "summary": "9 g hobby servo with signal, 5 V and ground. A 0.5 ms high holds the shaft at 0° and a 2.4 ms high at 180°, and a pulse past those stops clamps. The sheet's 1 ms to 2 ms is the nominal range around centre. It slews at 0.12 s per 60° on 4.8 V or more, holds when it arrives, and stays where it is when the pulses stop. From 2.3 V up to 4.5 V it moves slower and warns, unless the supply has already fallen below 2.3 V, in which case it stays stopped until the supply is back at 4.5 V. Below 2.3 V it does nothing. It draws 5 mA while it holds and 140 mA while it moves. A 3.3 V signal counts as a high. `angle` is the shaft in degrees, and the page turns the horn.",
