  "not_simulated": [
    { "what": "load and stall", "why": "Nothing pushes on the shaft, so the 1.8 kg·cm stall torque and the 520 mA stall current from the sheets are not states. The current is 140 mA while the shaft is moving and 5 mA while it holds." },
    { "what": "speed above 4.8 V", "why": "Tower Pro states 0.12 s per 60° at 4.8 V and no faster figure. At 4.5 V and above the shaft uses that speed, so a Nano's 5 V pin, which sits a diode drop under 5 V, does not warn. From 2.3 V up to 4.5 V the speed scales by the supply over 4.8 V and the part warns supply, unless the supply has already fallen below 2.3 V. Below 2.3 V, the AA51880 regulator's minimum output, the shaft stays put and the draw is none, and it stays stopped until the supply is back at 4.5 V." }
